<resources>
    <!--
        Android 15 (API 35) forces edge-to-edge on apps that target it, whether
        or not they call `enableEdgeToEdge()` — and with it, `adjustResize`
        stops working and the keyboard covers whatever is being typed into.

        This opts back out, which is supported for as long as the app targets
        35. When targetSdk moves to 36 the flag is ignored, and the app will
        have to consume `WindowInsets.ime` itself on every screen that takes
        input. That is a real piece of work, not a flag flip, and it should be
        done deliberately rather than discovered by an engineer who cannot see
        the serial they are typing.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.NaarniService" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowOptOutEdgeToEdgeEnforcement">true</item>
    </style>
</resources>
